// PauseDatabase parks a running cluster: the provisioner scales its
// pods to zero and keeps the storage, so a resume brings the same
// data back. Storage, backups, credentials and endpoints all survive
// — only the compute goes away.
//
// The request is ACCEPTED, not applied synchronously: if the cluster
// is mid-transition (version upgrade, failover, rolling restart) the
// operator parks it once that settles rather than tearing it down
